---
id: spinach-sun-dried-tomato-feta-egg-muffins
title: Spinach & Feta Egg Muffins
category: breakfast

yield:
  servings: 2
  cooked_g: 595

storage:
  fridge_days: 4
  freezer_friendly: true

---

Preheat the #oven to 190°C (375°F). Rub the insides of 8 cups of a #muffin-tin with @unsalted-butter{1/4%tsp}.

Thaw @frozen-chopped-spinach{1%nugget} in the #microwave for ~thaw{30%sec}, then squeeze it hard in your fist until no more water drips out; wet spinach makes watery muffins.

Lift @sun-dried-tomatoes-in-oil{3%tbsp} out of the jar with a fork, let the oil drip back, pat them with a paper towel, and chop. Crumble @greek-feta{40%g}, and put the rest of the block back under its brine.

Divide the spinach, tomatoes and feta between the 8 buttered cups.

In a #blender, blend @eggs{7}, @cottage-cheese-2pct{1/3%cup}, and @black-pepper{1/8%tsp} (no salt: the feta and tomatoes bring plenty) for ~blend{30%sec} until smooth. Pour it over the fillings, filling each cup almost to the top.

Bake for ~bake{18%minute}, until the centres no longer look wet and the edges are barely golden. Don't overbake, or they turn spongy. They puff up in the oven and settle as they cool. Loosen them with a knife and cool on a #wire-rack before refrigerating.

To serve, microwave 4 muffins for ~reheat{50%sec} and scatter thinly sliced @green-onions{1/8%bunch} on top, fresh, never baked. Have one @almond-hazelnut-biscotti{2} per breakfast with a flat white.
